<title>USA: Greyhound bus flips on highway in Illinois.</title>
<headline>Greyhound bus flips on highway in Illinois.</headline>
<dateline>RANTOUL, Ill. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Greyhound bus bound for Memphis from Chicago rolled over on an Interstate highway Thursday, injuring seven or eight people inside, Illinois State Police said.</p>
<p>None of the injuries was believed serious. It was not known if the driver was one of those hurt.</p>
<p>The accident happened on I-57 near Rantoul as the bus attempted to pass a truck, flipped on its side and slid into the northbound lanes of the road, police said.</p>
<p>The injured were taken to a hospital in Urbana, Illinois.</p>
